WEBVTT

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.130
Sis, it'll be all right.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.880
Thank you.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.090
I'm going to hang in there.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.300
Thank you, Sis.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.140
Excuse me.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.390
Oh, Mr. Kokubu.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.600
Miss, how are you feeling?

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.690
I’m really sorry.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.860
Um, I feel better now, so—

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.900
No, no, stay right there.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.740
Uh, Mr. Kokubu,
I was being quite rude earlier...

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.660
Um...

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:42.290
Miss, you have nothing at all to be sorry about.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.790
It's okay.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.790
More importantly...

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.010
Why don't we talk about what to do next?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.020
Small Palm

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.020
Hey, Mr. Kokubu...

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.030
How long are you
going to keep calling me here?

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.280
I mean...

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.290
didn't I already apologize?

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.790
Right?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.210
Yes. With your words.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.460
<i>I'm sorry for what I did.</i>

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:03.890
I apologized and I'm keeping
my mouth shut in class.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.390
Isn't that enough?

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.690
Part of the work
is becoming aware of what you did.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.150
What'll happen if I become aware of it?

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.910
Will something change?

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.910
If something changes,
will I get something good out of it?

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:32.880
Tell me, Mr. Kokubu,
will something good happen if we keep living?

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.630
My parents and everyone around me

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.970
say do your best and study hard
so you can get into a good high school,

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.680
but even if I got into a good school,
who's to say I'll get a job at all,

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.640
let alone one at a good company?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.190
"If you do your best, you'll get good results,"

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.570
but there's no guarantee of that,
and still people say, "Do your best!"

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.360
Isn't that crazy?

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.450
It's like, if I worked as hard as I could,
but it didn't work out,

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.450
nobody's going to take responsibility.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.210
I see.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.710
So you're nervous about the future
because of that.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.130
And your parents don't understand you.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.180
Hm, hmm.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.930
So?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:31.270
What part of that has anything to do
with Kawamoto and Sakura?

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.060
Absolutely nothing, right?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.650
Stop talking like you've come to the conclusion
that it's all society's fault.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.700
Keep it up and I'll start talking about life
in Japan when I was a kid.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.410
The postwar period!
It was still postwar times!

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:52.210
If I did that, you'd be like,
"That has nothing to do with this." Sheesh!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.090
You wouldn't understand how I feel.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.090
That's why I'm asking now!

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.300
Let's talk!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.100
All right. The perilla plant is set.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.600
We can put the basil next to it.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.570
And let's put the mint somewhere else.
It grows too much.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:20.780
Right.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.900
Now let's give them plenty of water.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.570
Okay.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:35.290
<i>Last week in homeroom, Mr. Kokubu said
something to the class with a clear voice.</i>

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:43.510
Okay, today there are several things
I want to ask you.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:51.260
First, Arai, Takashi, Kimura,
Mochizuki, Takagi, and Wakabayashi.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.390
There are individual questions for you six,

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:58.860
so you'll each go with a teacher
to another classroom.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.780
<i>That's when everyone in the class realized.</i>

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:10.660
<i>The school had gotten serious
about intervening in the darkness in our class.</i>

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:16.790
<i>Now we knew this teacher wasn't just
going through the motions of doing something.</i>

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.290
Okay.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.300
I guess we'll get started here.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.220
So...

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:31.010
Tell me what's really going on.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.810
<i>The unwritten rules that had spread in our class</i>

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.810
<i>wouldn't work anymore from now on.</i>

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:46.490
<i>Everyone realized that
maybe the days of living in fear</i>

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:51.120
<i>of becoming the next target may now be over.</i>

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.090
<i>And so, the curtain came down.</i>

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.340
Um, I apologize.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.350
- I'm sorry.
- I apologize.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:17.850
<i>With words that made it hard to tell
if it was really over at all.</i>

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.650
There wasn't one bit of sincerity in that.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.820
It seems we've still got a long way to go.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.170
Mr. Kokubu, is it okay if I don't forgive them?

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:50.590
Just, "apologize and you'll be forgiven,"
with no punishment given.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.930
When I think about
how Chiho had to change schools...

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.560
It's too much to forgive.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:01.520
"Compassion"?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.320
Hmm, I'm kind of drawing a blank.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.190
Is that like "hypocrisy"?

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.870
It's like something you need, or what?

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.420
"Education" huh?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.550
If only it were as easy as it sounds.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.350
Our job is to "teach" and "raise" students.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:44.400
Take "raise" out of the equation,
and I would never have gotten involved...

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.110
in this whole issue.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.280
<i>Snore snore...</i>

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.830
<i>Wheeze...</i>

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:12.670
Hina!

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.260
MS. HINATA KAWAMOTO

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.270
FROM CHIHO SAKURA

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.980
It's from Chiho!

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.480
<i>Hina, I'm sorry it's taken me so long
to get back to you.</i>

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:41.660
<i>Right now, I'm studying with a teacher
in a place called a "Heart Care Center."</i>

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:51.760
<i>It's a quiet, pretty area
surrounded by mountains and forests.</i>

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.720
<i>There's a ranch and farm next to the center.</i>

00:09:56.180 --> 00:10:01.060
<i>They let me help out there sometimes.</i>

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.110
<i>This is a baby goat that was born on the ranch.</i>

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:11.940
<i>Her name is Mei.</i>

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.070
<i>The dog to my left is Hana.</i>

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:19.780
<i>They always come running over
to see me when I go to the ranch.</i>

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.700
<i>They're the first friends I made here.</i>

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:33.090
<i>All of the people on the farm and ranch
are very friendly.</i>

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.090
<i>The people in the neighborhood, too.</i>

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:44.470
<i>The other day, we made plum wine,
plum syrup, and plum jam together.</i>

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.060
<i>My mom helped too,
and we had a good time.</i>

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:02.870
<i>My dad's office isn't too far from the center,
so he drops me off and picks me up every day.</i>

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:13.460
<i>I'm really happy to have more chances
to talk to him now.</i>

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:25.310
<i>When I first came here, I couldn't get used to
this new place, so I was really lonely.</i>

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:40.950
<i>But then Ms. Satou, my teacher at the center,
taught me the "three steps to making a friend."</i>

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:47.660
<i>You start by making friends with animals.</i>

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:52.670
<i>After you do that, the next step is making friends
with people who are older than you.</i>

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.670
<i>And today...</i>

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:02.180
TO MS. SATOU

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:12.560
<i>Ms. Satou said,
"Why don't we move on to the third step?"</i>

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:18.690
<i>The third step is making friends with someone
who's close to your own age.</i>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.700
<i>When I heard that...</i>

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.710
<i>I thought about you, Hina.</i>

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.510
<i>I really miss you.</i>

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:49.430
<i>When the plum syrup is just right,
I'd like to drink some with you.</i>

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.560
<i>I planted corn too.</i>

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.650
<i>It'll be ready to pick by August.</i>

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.610
<i>I'd like to eat the corn with you.</i>

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.250
<i>Will you come and visit me
during summer vacation?</i>

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.630
<i>Can I look forward to seeing you?</i>

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.470
<i>From Chiho</i>

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.020
Small Palm

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:34.020
In the Sun

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.400
TSUKUDAKO BRIDGE

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:45.910
Hello!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.300
Pardon me.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.450
<i>She's sleeping.</i>

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:48.970
Wants to go in, but can't.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:48.970
Unsure if it's okay to enter
a house where a girl's sleeping

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:52.430
Ooph...

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.730
Sat down for now...

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:10.870
<i>I wonder why.</i>

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:16.000
<i>For the first time in a while,
it's like she has a soft aura around her.</i>

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:21.670
<i>Like she's faintly glowing...</i>

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.550
<i>Feels like I could look at her like this forever.</i>

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.190
<i>Rei...</i>

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:46.900
<i>Rei.</i>

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.400
Rei!

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.160
Apparently nodded off

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.240
Summer tangerines!

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:56.910
And so many of them!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.250
My workshop mentor gave them to me.
He picked a ton, so told me to take them.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:04.920
<i>I can't believe I fell asleep on her doorstep.</i>

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.510
Oh, wow!

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.260
So many...

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.930
Wait, all of them?

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.510
What about you, Mr. Shimada?

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.510
It grew on your property,
but you won't eat any?

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:21.020
Nah, I have a feeling the acid in the tangerines
would melt through my stomach lining.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:25.070
There are no pesticides on them,
so you can make jam and stuff.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.570
I can't, though.

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:29.530
HAHAHA...

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:28.780
Jam?

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:28.780
JAM?

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:29.530
OH

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.070
Akari.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:34.530
<i>You're saving me money on groceries again!
I'll make jam!</i>

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.620
It smells good.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:45.040
This'll be great.
Sis's marmalade is delicious.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:50.800
<i>Just as I thought, she's faintly glowing...</i>

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.050
<i>I wonder why.</i>

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:08.480
Kiriyama, actually...

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.070
It seems like it's over.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:19.490
I think it's over.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:22.460
Probably...

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.250
<i>I see. That must be why...</i>

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.420
<i>she's glowing.</i>

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.030
Cute, aren't they?

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:54.530
We baked them yesterday
at my classmate Kawashima's house.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.530
We're in the same group.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:02.040
It was me, Kawashima, Kiuchi,
Kobayashi and Kudou, so five of us.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:05.790
Kawamoto.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:12.550
So we're going to make cookies today
at Kawashima's house.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.430
Want to join us?

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.470
Um...

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.480
I'm sorry!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.690
I-I was scared.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.940
That's why I couldn't do anything.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:37.700
Even if we apologize, we thought that...

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.830
you might not forgive us.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:46.710
But I really wanted to apologize to you.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.920
<i>After that, I changed clothes,</i>

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:57.220
<i>then met up with the girls
at Kawashima's house.</i>

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:05.180
<i>We baked a lot of cookies together.</i>

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:30.000
<i>The cookies turned out hard and misshapen...</i>

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.600
What is this? It's awful!

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:49.980
<i>After I said that, we couldn't stop laughing.</i>

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:56.030
<i>While we were laughing, we said,
"Still, cookies right out of the oven are good,"</i>

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.030
<i>and we kept on eating them.</i>

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.070
<i>I wonder why.</i>

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:05.990
<i>Store-bought cookies taste much better,</i>

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:11.540
<i>but I had such a good time
and was so happy that they were delicious.</i>

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:17.260
Kiriyama, did you know?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:21.510
When you put a cookie fresh from the oven
to your mouth, it sizzles?

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:23.720
I burned the inside of my mouth.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:24.890
Look!

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:32.520
<i>Saying that, she innocently
opened her mouth wide.</i>

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:36.190
<i>When I saw the sunlight
on her teeth and tongue,</i>

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:40.950
<i>for some reason
various feelings welled up inside.</i>

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:46.580
<i>I had a tightening sensation in my chest
and felt like I was going to cry.</i>

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.460
Hina, I'm sorry.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:53.460
I...

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.510
In the end, I couldn't do anything.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:05.550
<i>That's right. Even though I promised right here</i>

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:09.640
<i>that I would protect you that day.</i>

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:16.820
Nothing?

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:28.990
Kiriyama...

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:32.620
Even though...

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:35.250
Even though you listened...

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:37.590
to me...

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.590
all those times?

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:46.720
Even though you went to Kyoto
to search for me?

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.560
Even though you made me so happy?

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.100
After all, I wasn't able to...

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:56.060
Ow!

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.480
Don't give me, "After all!"

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:58.270
EHHH

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:00.230
B-But I...

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:01.860
No buts!

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.490
Kiriyama, you're an idiot!

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:04.740
Ouch!

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:04.740
CHOMP

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.240
Oh, that's right! Guess what!

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.410
I got a letter from Chiho!

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:15.330
From Chiho? Really?

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:17.670
And then, and then!

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:22.880
During summer vacation,
I'm going to visit her, for sure!

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:27.050
<i>While telling me that, she pulled me
by the hand as if we were dancing,</i>

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:29.970
<i>and started walking at a steady pace.</i>

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>And to this small heroine who never gave in,
no matter how much she cried or suffered,</i>

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.690
<i>I made another promise,</i>

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:55.410
<i>and a little oath of loyalty in my head.</i>

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.040
In the Sun

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:36.770
Episode 36

00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:35.350
What is this?
What is this poster?

00:24:35.350 --> 00:24:37.680
The design is really cool.

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:39.020
It's my fault?!

00:24:39.430 --> 00:24:40.350
Yes.

00:24:40.350 --> 00:24:43.150
But for some reason,
it doesn't feel real.

00:24:43.150 --> 00:24:45.320
Did you tell her that?

00:24:45.650 --> 00:24:47.480
It's easy to figure out.

00:24:47.650 --> 00:24:50.030
Because you've been listening
to her all this time.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
AKIO WATANABE

00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:52.990
Maybe I'll have Sis tell me

00:24:52.990 --> 00:24:55.580
how to make marmalade
so I can make it, too!
